  <prompt>
    Write the part-merge seam test that proves a document merged through a firm/matter template CARRIES THAT TEMPLATE'S
    CHROME — assert the provenance of `styles.xml`, `sectPr`, and the header/footer parts on the merged output (they
    come from the template, not the editor body). This is Success Criterion 3. Use an ADR-038 seam / KEEP-path vertical
    slice over the REAL 030 part-merge engine (built in 030) — NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration
    test, NO ctor-null test. Also record the Placement Justification + §11 Component Justification for the Phase 3
    part-merge component in the PR / project notes.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer writing an integration/seam test over the OOXML part-merge engine. Expert in ADR-038's KEEP-path seam model (real components, no `Mock&lt;...&gt;`, no DI/ctor tests) and in inspecting OOXML parts (`StyleDefinitionsPart`, `SectionProperties`, `HeaderPart`/`FooterPart`) to assert provenance. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    A seam test at the `tests/integration/seam/Compose/**` KEEP path that merges an editor body through a firm/matter
    `.dotx` via the real 030 engine and asserts: the merged `styles.xml` / `sectPr` / header-footer parts come from the
    template (chrome provenance), while the body content comes from the editor. Fails loudly if any chrome part is the
    editor's rather than the template's. The Placement + §11 Component Justification for the part-merge component is
    recorded in the PR / notes.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Success Criterion 3: "A document merged through a firm template carries that template's headers/footers/styles —
      verify by a part-merge integration test asserting `styles.xml`/`sectPr`/header-footer provenance." Task 030 built
      the engine; 032 wired it. This task is the standing regression net proving the merge adopts the template's chrome
      (not the body's). Because it exercises the real `Services/Compose/` engine with no mocks, it is an ADR-038 seam
      vertical slice. Per spec §11, the part-merge component's Placement + Component Justification is also documented here.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ — the part-merge chrome-provenance seam test (merge body → firm `.dotx`; assert `styles.xml`/`sectPr`/header-footer come from the template).</file>
