  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / Success Criterion 3">The test MUST assert `styles.xml` / `sectPr` / header-footer provenance on the merged output — the chrome comes from the template, the body from the editor. Scope: use a firm/matter `.dotx` with DISTINCTIVE chrome so provenance is unambiguous.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">The test is a seam / KEEP-path vertical slice over the REAL 030 engine. Scope: NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration test, NO ctor-null test — drive the actual part-merge engine end-to-end at `tests/integration/seam/Compose/**`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / ADR-013">The test exercises pure `Services/Compose/` code (`byte[]`/OOXML in, projection out). Scope: no `Microsoft.Graph`, no AI-internal type in the test path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §11">Record the Placement Justification + Component Justification for the part-merge component (existing = `WordTemplateService` text-only + none for part-merge; extension = No + why; cost-of-doing-nothing = cannot apply house style, Success Criterion 3 fails) in the PR / notes. Scope: documentation obligation, cited in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / BFF Hygiene §10">No runtime package added. Scope: `dotnet publish -c Release` unaffected — report size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expect ~0); `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

