  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor declaration: 🔒 RIGOR LEVEL: STANDARD (plan.md §5) / 📋 REASON: test-modifying `tests/**` → TEST-MODIFYING override (root §8) makes Step 9.5 gates UNCONDITIONAL / 📖 PROTOCOL STEPS. Load Success Criterion 3, §11, ADR-038.</step>
    <step order="1" name="RE-GREP the seam path + fixtures">Confirm the established `tests/integration/seam/Compose/**` path and pick a corpus body doc + a firm/matter `.dotx` with distinctive chrome (styles/sectPr/headers-footers).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Write the provenance seam test">Merge the body through the `.dotx` via the real 030 engine; open the merged package; assert `styles.xml` / `sectPr` / header-footer parts come from the template and the body paragraphs from the editor. No banned mock/DI/ctor tests.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Record justification + build">Record the Placement + §11 Component Justification for the part-merge component in the PR/notes. `dotnet test` the seam suite green; `dotnet publish -c Release` size + delta (0). `/conflict-check` before the PR.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Close out">Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set task 033 to ✅. Record any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the merged output's chrome (`styles.xml`/`sectPr`/header-footer) does NOT come from the template — STOP. Do NOT weaken the assertion to make the test pass; surface WHICH part is wrong (template vs editor provenance) so 030 is fixed. A green test that hides missing template chrome would falsely satisfy Success Criterion 3.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run the seam test suite; `dotnet publish -c Release` for the size check.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ — part-merge chrome-provenance seam test (styles.xml/sectPr/header-footer provenance)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an editor body merged through a firm/matter `.dotx` via the real 030 engine, when the merged package is inspected, then `styles.xml`, `sectPr`, and the header/footer parts come from the template.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The merged body paragraphs are the editor's content (body provenance), confirming the merge combined template chrome + editor body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test is an ADR-038 seam / KEEP-path slice over the real engine — no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration test, no ctor-null test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if any chrome part is the editor's rather than the template's, the test FAILS loudly (and the escalation fires) — the assertion is not weakened.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Placement + §11 Component Justification for the part-merge component is recorded in the PR / notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet test` seam suite green; publish size ~0 MB delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline; `/conflict-check` clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">TASK-INDEX.md shows task 033 as ✅ and any deviation is recorded in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <completion-note>COMPLETED 2026-08-07 (isolated-worktree agent; cherry-picked 77e4d9dfc). ComposeTemplateChromeProvenanceSeamTests (1 file, 3 facts) — gap-fill vs 030/032 coverage (assessment table in agent report): NEW at the wire: styles.xml provenance (contested Heading1 — template color wins on PERSISTED bytes; FirmBody survives), footer part via sectPr FooterReference, OpenXmlValidator on wire bytes, no-dangling-rId scans, mergeWarnings-empty assertions; PLUS the notes-§21 imported-carrier slices on REAL corpus docs: multi-author-redline-synthetic (ins/del authors, delText, rPrChange/pPrChange, mark-deletion, tracked hyperlink rel by URI, grafted anchored comment carried) and nda-interrupted-clauses (real numId collision remapped, template UpperRoman intact, table carried, real Heading1 collision template-wins). Suite 1069/1069 single-run. FIXTURE FINDING (not production): nda-interrupted-clauses.docx carries 8 pre-existing spec-invalid w14:paraId >= 0x80000000 — NDA slice uses baseline-diff validator (self-destructs to strict when fixture cleaned); fixture regeneration recommended at wrap-up. Placement + §11 justification recorded in notes §23. Step 9.5 lean review launched on the merged SHA.</completion-note>
